    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d761">

                <pb facs="0843" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.5151/151</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Latin
                        American Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-08-12">August 12, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Last night Dr. Espil, the Argentine Ambassador, told me that the group in New
                    York which had negotiated the exchange agreement with the Bank of Brazil<anchor
                        n="32" xml:id="d761-f1"/> had communicated with him about the possibility of
                    discussing an arrangement to liberate American frozen commercial credits in
                    Argentina. Representatives of the group are coming down to talk with him the
                    first of next week. Dr. Espil said that he had no instructions from his
                    Government and intended only to listen.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin C. Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
